{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed residential units would be provided with unsatisfactory levels of natural light and outlook due to the poor design of the development. This would give rise to substandard poor quality accommodation and general environment to the detriment of the residential amenities of future occupiers contrary to Policies D3 and D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Documents Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development by reason of its poor design, size, scale, proportions and siting would appear contrived, cramped and out of keeping with the wider pattern of development to the detriment of the character and appearance of the surrounding area. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the high-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 and D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010) and Policy GR1 of the emerging Local Plan.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
